*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*%
*% PPD file for Epilog Zing 24 Laser Engraver
*% For use with macOS CUPS printing system
*%

*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*FileVersion: "1.0"
*LanguageVersion: English
*LanguageEncoding: ISOLatin1
*PCFileName: "EPLZING24.PPD"
*Manufacturer: "Epilog"
*Product: "(Epilog Zing 24)"
*ModelName: "Epilog Zing 24"
*ShortNickName: "Epilog Zing 24"
*NickName: "Epilog Zing 24 Laser Engraver"
*PSVersion: "(3010.000) 0"
*LanguageLevel: "3"
*% The laser is monochrome, but the driver routes cuts by COLOR: strokes in
*% red/green/blue/cyan/yellow/magenta become vector cuts, everything else is
*% engraved. Declaring a Gray device makes macOS convert all color to
*% greyscale before spooling, which destroys that information (cyan arrives
*% as white). So the device must advertise RGB even though the laser is not
*% a color printer.
*ColorDevice: True
*DefaultColorSpace: RGB

*% Take colour matching into our own hands. Without this macOS colour-manages
*% the document into the device's colourspace before the filter runs, and a
*% laser is a one-component device, so cut colours arrive as white or grey.
*% Per Apple's PPD extensions the handoff colourspace follows the component
*% count the driver requests; declaring custom matching with an RGB profile
*% gets the document delivered with its colour intact, which this driver needs
*% because it routes cuts by colour.
*APSupportsCustomColorMatching: True
*APDefaultCustomColorMatchingProfile: sRGB
*APCustomColorMatchingProfile: sRGB
*APCustomColorMatchingProfile: AdobeRGB
*APCustomColorMatchingProfile: GenericRGB
*FileSystem: False
*Throughput: "1"
*TTRasterizer: Type42
*1284DeviceID: "MFG:Epilog;MDL:Zing 24;CMD:PJL,PCL,HPGL;"

*% Filter declarations - Accept PDF directly for vector support
*% PDF preferred (lower cost) - preserves vector paths for HPGL cutting
*cupsFilter2: "application/pdf application/vnd.epilog 50 rastertoepiloz"
*% CUPS raster fallback for compatibility
*cupsFilter2: "application/vnd.cups-raster application/vnd.epilog 100 rastertoepiloz"

*% Colour mode. The laser is monochrome, but cut routing is done by colour, so
*% the spooled data must stay RGB. Without a ColorModel option macOS has no
*% colour choice to make and converts everything to greyscale, which turns a
*% cyan cut line into pure white before the driver ever sees it.
*OpenUI *ColorModel/Color Mode: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 5 AnySetup *ColorModel
*DefaultColorModel: RGB
*ColorModel RGB/Color (required for vector cutting): "<</cupsColorSpace 1 /cupsColorOrder 0 /cupsBitsPerColor 8 /cupsBitsPerPixel 24>>setpagedevice"
*ColorModel Gray/Grayscale (engrave only): "<</cupsColorSpace 3 /cupsColorOrder 0 /cupsBitsPerColor 8 /cupsBitsPerPixel 8>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *ColorModel

*% Supported resolutions (from EpilogZing.java)
*OpenUI *Resolution/Resolution: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *Resolution
*DefaultResolution: 500dpi
*Resolution 100dpi/100 DPI: "<</HWResolution[100 100]>>setpagedevice"
*Resolution 200dpi/200 DPI: "<</HWResolution[200 200]>>setpagedevice"
*Resolution 250dpi/250 DPI: "<</HWResolution[250 250]>>setpagedevice"
*Resolution 400dpi/400 DPI: "<</HWResolution[400 400]>>setpagedevice"
*Resolution 500dpi/500 DPI (Recommended): "<</HWResolution[500 500]>>setpagedevice"
*Resolution 1000dpi/1000 DPI: "<</HWResolution[1000 1000]>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *Resolution

*% Raster Power (0-100%)
*OpenUI *RasterPower/Raster Power: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 20 AnySetup *RasterPower
*DefaultRasterPower: 100
*RasterPower 0/0% (Off): ""
*RasterPower 10/10%: ""
*RasterPower 20/20%: ""
*RasterPower 30/30%: ""
*RasterPower 40/40%: ""
*RasterPower 50/50%: ""
*RasterPower 60/60%: ""
*RasterPower 70/70%: ""
*RasterPower 80/80%: ""
*RasterPower 90/90%: ""
*RasterPower 100/100%: ""
*CloseUI: *RasterPower

