*OrderDependency: 23 AnySetup *VectorSpeed
*DefaultVectorSpeed: 100
*VectorSpeed 10/10%: ""
*VectorSpeed 20/20%: ""
*VectorSpeed 30/30%: ""
*VectorSpeed 40/40%: ""
*VectorSpeed 50/50%: ""
*VectorSpeed 60/60%: ""
*VectorSpeed 70/70%: ""
*VectorSpeed 80/80%: ""
*VectorSpeed 90/90%: ""
*VectorSpeed 100/100%: ""
*CloseUI: *VectorSpeed

*% Vector Frequency (1-5000 Hz)
*OpenUI *VectorFrequency/Vector Frequency: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 24 AnySetup *VectorFrequency
*DefaultVectorFrequency: 5000
*VectorFrequency 500/500 Hz: ""
*VectorFrequency 1000/1000 Hz: ""
*VectorFrequency 2000/2000 Hz: ""
*VectorFrequency 2500/2500 Hz: ""
*VectorFrequency 3000/3000 Hz: ""
*VectorFrequency 4000/4000 Hz: ""
*VectorFrequency 5000/5000 Hz: ""
*CloseUI: *VectorFrequency

*% Test Frame - trace where the job will land so material can be positioned.
*% Run once with this on, watch the head, move the stock, then run again with
*% it off to do the real job. Overrides Job Type: no engraving or cutting is
*% performed, only the outline pass.
*OpenUI *TestFrame/Test Frame: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 24 AnySetup *TestFrame
*DefaultTestFrame: Off
*TestFrame Off/Off - run the real job: ""
*TestFrame Trace/Trace outline - laser off, lid may stay open: ""
*TestFrame Mark/Mark outline - low power, lid must be closed: ""
*CloseUI: *TestFrame

*% Job Type
*OpenUI *JobType/Job Type: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 25 AnySetup *JobType
*DefaultJobType: Combined
*JobType Raster/Raster Only: ""
*JobType Vector/Vector Only: ""
*JobType Combined/Combined (Raster + Vector): ""
*CloseUI: *JobType

*% Dithering - how continuous tone becomes on/off laser dots. A laser fires or
*% it does not, so a photograph must be rendered as a pattern of dots whose
*% density stands in for brightness. None is correct for line art and vector
*% artwork, where dithering only fuzzes clean edges; the diffusion modes are for
*% photographs and gradients, which a plain threshold destroys.
*OpenUI *Dithering/Dithering: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 27 AnySetup *Dithering
*DefaultDithering: None
*Dithering None/None - line art and text: ""
*Dithering Ordered/Ordered (Bayer) - even texture: ""
*Dithering FloydSteinberg/Floyd-Steinberg - photographs: ""
*Dithering Jarvis/Jarvis - smoother gradients: ""
*Dithering Stucki/Stucki - smooth, slightly crisper: ""
*CloseUI: *Dithering

*% Raster Mode (1-bit bitmap vs 8-bit greyscale 3D)
*OpenUI *RasterMode/Raster Mode: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 26 AnySetup *RasterMode
*DefaultRasterMode: Bitmap
*% These choices carry no setpagedevice. They previously set cupsColorSpace 3
*% (K, one component), and because RasterMode is ordered after ColorModel that
*% silently overrode the colour model - macOS saw a driver asking for one
*% component, handed off GenericGray, and every cut colour arrived as white.
*% Those attributes only ever applied to the CUPS raster path, which this driver
*% does not use: it consumes application/pdf directly. The filter takes the
*% raster bit depth from the RasterMode option name itself.
*RasterMode Bitmap/Standard (1-bit): ""
*RasterMode Greyscale3D/3D Greyscale (8-bit): ""
*CloseUI: *RasterMode

*% Engrave Direction
*OpenUI *EngraveBottomUp/Engrave Direction: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 27 AnySetup *EngraveBottomUp
*DefaultEngraveBottomUp: false
*EngraveBottomUp false/Top to Bottom: ""
*EngraveBottomUp true/Bottom to Top: ""
*CloseUI: *EngraveBottomUp

*% Autofocus
*OpenUI *AutoFocus/Auto Focus: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 28 AnySetup *AutoFocus
*DefaultAutoFocus: false
*AutoFocus false/Off: ""
*AutoFocus true/On: ""
*CloseUI: *AutoFocus

*% Focus Adjustment (manual focus offset in mm, -12.7 to +12.7)
*OpenUI *Focus/Focus Offset (mm): PickOne
*OrderDependency: 29 AnySetup *Focus
*DefaultFocus: 0
*Focus -10/-10.0 mm: ""
*Focus -5/-5.0 mm: ""
*Focus -2/-2.0 mm: ""
*Focus -1/-1.0 mm: ""
*Focus 0/0 mm (Default): ""
*Focus 1/+1.0 mm: ""
*Focus 2/+2.0 mm: ""
*Focus 5/+5.0 mm: ""
*Focus 10/+10.0 mm: ""
*CloseUI: *Focus

